[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pulls/1","id":5130256413,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVbUqvc8AAAABMcmAHQ","html_url":"https://github.com/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pull/1.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/1","number":1,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add Experiment 5 scorer: read a reply into a network and score it on MinAtar","user":{"login":"suitedaces","id":50865782,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODY1Nzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50865782?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces","html_url":"https://github.com/suitedaces","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The release has the Experiment 5 replies, networks and scores, but no code to read a reply into a network or to score a network. This adds `exp5_write_from_scratch/code/score.py` and a short section in that folder's README.\n\n**What it does**\n- Reads a reply the way the prompt describes: only the last `edits` block, statements in order, a statement that cannot be read is skipped. It accepts the `[ [ ... ] ]` form mentioned in the README.\n- Scores a network with the protocol in the prompt: MinAtar 1.0.15, sticky actions 0.1, actions sampled from the softmax, at most 10,000 steps, 1,000 episodes. It prints the same fields as `eval/minatar_eval.json`.\n- `--save` writes the network read from a reply in the `hand.npz` format.\n\n**Checks**\n- Reading `runs/<game>/reply/answer.md` gives `networks/<game>/hand.npz` exactly (float32-identical), with the same statement counts as `apply.json` (92 / 122 / 55, 0 errors).\n- Scoring the released networks (seed 0):\n\n| Game | `eval/minatar_eval.json` | `code/score.py` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Breakout | 517.4 ± 7.4 | 502.8 ± 7.7 |\n| Seaquest | 53.1 ± 1.4 | 52.6 ± 1.4 |\n| Asterix | 53.2 ± 1.0 | 52.4 ± 1.0 |\n\nThe differences are within episode noise (different random streams for the game and the action sampling). If your scorer did anything differently, for example resetting `last_action` between episodes or a different seeding scheme, I'm happy to match it.\n","created_at":"2026-11-03T01:27:23Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T01:31:56Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1e82eafd331a262bbade1449e5635c9ae0fd8f82","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pulls/1/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pulls/1/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/1/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/statuses/d85e03712bcf24e3b5c45c80889c6a106b8cb2e0","head":{"label":"suitedaces:exp5-score","ref":"exp5-score","sha":"d85e03712bcf24e3b5c45c80889c6a106b8cb2e0","user":{"login":"suitedaces","id":50865782,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODY1Nzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50865782?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://ap